# venueplay.com.au cache rules (Cloudflare Pages).
#
# This site had no _headers file, which is why new deploys only showed up in an
# incognito window: browsers were serving the old cached HTML. The rule below makes
# every page and app file revalidate with the server before it is used, so venues
# always get the latest version (a quick 304 when nothing changed).
#
# We use "no-cache" (revalidate), not "no-store" (never cache), on purpose: the home
# page and the musical game load /data/musical-library.json in the browser, and
# no-store would force that whole file to download again every single time.

/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate
  # Basic hardening. SAMEORIGIN rather than DENY because /tv embeds the game screens
  # in an iframe from this same site, and DENY would black out the venue TV.
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains

# Shared scripts must revalidate like the pages that load them.
#
# The /* rule above did NOT reach them: Cloudflare Pages was serving /app/vp-session.js with
# max-age=14400 while every .html on the site correctly said no-cache. So a fix to the shared
# session library sat invisible in browsers for four hours after it went live, which is exactly
# how the empty HQ venue list survived its own fix. A more specific rule wins, so name them.
/*.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate
/app/*.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate

# Brand logos never change under a given filename, so cache them hard for a year.
/logos/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
